# AppleDocsTool Skills (Cursor)

Use the repository skills as the default workflow source for Apple development tasks.

## Discovery

1. Read `skills/SKILLS.md` first to select the right capability.
2. Read only the relevant `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`.
3. Execute shell commands from the selected skill directly.

## Skill Selection

- `skills/analyze-project/SKILL.md`: project structure, symbols, dependencies.
- `skills/build-and-test/SKILL.md`: build/test flows and failure debugging.
- `skills/lookup-docs/SKILL.md`: Apple API and dependency docs lookup.
- `skills/control-simulator/SKILL.md`: simulator lifecycle and app/device control.
- `skills/profile-app/SKILL.md`: Instruments and performance profiling.
- `skills/ui-interact/SKILL.md`: UI automation and visual-state interactions.

## Execution Rules

1. Prefer shell-first workflows (`swift`, `xcodebuild`, `xcrun simctl`, `xcrun xctrace`).
2. Use MCP tools when shell commands are insufficient:
   - structured symbol/doc output
   - simulator OCR and coordinate-based UI interactions
3. For UI automation tasks, prefer `apple-docs` MCP tools from `.cursor/mcp.json`.
4. Keep context small: load only the files and sections needed for the current task.
